Project 2: Sales Insights Dashboard

What it is. An interactive dashboard built on a real public dataset, for example a retail or online
shopping sales dataset from Kaggle. It answers real business questions: which products and regions sell
most, how sales change by month, who the best customers are, and what should the business do next.
Why it impresses. It turns your existing Pandas, Matplotlib and Seaborn knowledge into something a
recruiter can actually open and use. It also directly supports your Data Analyst backup path. The
difference between a beginner and a strong candidate here is the written insights, not the number of
charts.

Tech stack
       
Part                             Use

Data                             A public sales dataset from Kaggle (kaggle.com/datasets)
Analysis                         Pandas and NumPy, in a Jupyter notebook first
Charts                           Matplotlib and Seaborn in the notebook, Plotly for interactive charts in the app
App                              Streamlit (streamlit.io)
Storage                          CSV at first, then load the cleaned data into PostgreSQL and query it with SQL

Must have features
• A cleaning notebook that documents every step: missing values, duplicates, wrong data types,
outliers.
• KPI cards: total revenue, total orders, average order value, number of customers.
• Monthly trend, top ten products, sales by region and category.
• Filters by date range, region and category.
• A written insights section with five to seven findings and a recommendation for each.

Extra features once the basics work
• Customer segmentation using RFM analysis (recency, frequency, monetary).
• A simple sales forecast for the next three months.
• Rebuild the same dashboard in Power BI and compare. Useful if you lean towards the analyst role.

