• Write the SQL for the top three products in each region (window functions).

Requirements Details

 Sales Insights Dashboard, you need to shift your focus from simply writing code to thinking like a data-driven business consultant. Recruiters look at this project to see if you can translate raw messy numbers into actionable revenue-generating strategies.
Because this project spans across both exploratory data science and relational database querying, your preparation must focus on advanced analytical methods, professional visualization techniques, and intermediate SQL.

1. Data Cleaning & Statistical Integrity (Pandas & NumPy)

Data cleaning is the most critical conversation you will have in a technical interview. You need to know how to fix bad data without introducing statistical bias.
• Outlier Profiling: Learn how to use the Interquartile Range (IQR) method or Z-scores to isolate transaction outliers (e.g., separating an actual wholesale corporate order from a data entry typo).
• Missing Value Strategies: Learn when to drop rows versus when to impute values (filling fields using median/mode group mapping), and how to document this process clearly in markdown text.
• Vectorized Data Transformation: Master casting string text to true datetime objects (pd.to_datetime) and creating conditional columns efficiently using np.select or np.where.

2. Intermediate SQL & Window Functions (PostgreSQL)

A major milestone of this project is moving your calculations from Python dataframes into a SQL database. Recruiters will test your raw query skills.
• SQL Window Functions: Master using ROW_NUMBER(), RANK(), and DENSE_RANK() paired with OVER (PARTITION BY region ORDER BY revenue DESC) to find top-performing items dynamically across different zones.
• Advanced Aggregations: Learn how to write complex queries utilizing CASE WHEN clauses to pivot text data, alongside structural grouping operators (GROUP BY, HAVING).
• Common Table Expressions (CTEs): Learn how to structure long, complicated analytical queries using WITH statements so they are readable and optimized.

3. Business Analytics & Frameworks

The differentiator between a basic student dashboard and an advanced portfolio piece is the sophistication of the business analysis.
• RFM Segmentation Matrix: Understand the mathematical logic behind Recency, Frequency, and Monetary analysis to bin customers into explicit action tiers (e.g., "Champions," "At Risk," "Hibernating").
• Translating Metrics to Decisions: Learn what executive-level KPIs mean conceptually—such as how Average Order Value (AOV) changes relative to Order Volume, and how to write clear business recommendations.

4. Interactive UI Engineering (Streamlit & Plotly)

You need to build a web application that remains fast and interactive even when sorting through thousands of sales transactions.
• State & Filter Management: Learn how to use Streamlit control flow widgets (st.sidebar.selectbox, st.date_input) to dynamically slice and filter a global Pandas dataframe object.
• Interactive Charting Engines: Learn how to configure Plotly Express charts (px.line, px.bar) to build tooltips and hover effects, replacing static images with dynamic visual fields.

